{"term":"equal","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5e8a3772d995091582","definition":"The same in one or more respects.","example":"Near-synonyms: equivalent; see also Thesaurus:equal","pos":"adj","synonyms":["equivalent"],"antonyms":["unequal"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, usually","register":"not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":["balanced"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cf69faa72dd9593253","definition":"Fair, impartial.","example":"it could not but much redound to the lustre of your milde and equall Government, when as private persons are hereby animated to thinke ye better pleas'd with publick advice, then other statists have been delighted heretofore with publicke flattery.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["objective","unbiased","candid","cold","clinical","detached","egal","equal","equitable","evenhanded","fairhanded","fair-minded","disinterested","dispassionate","impartial","imprejudicate","indifferent","indistinguishing","neuter","neutral","nonaligned","nonpartial","nonpartisan","nonpersonal","objective","unbiased","unbigoted","uninterested","unpartial","unpartisan","unprejudiced","unprepossessed"],"antonyms":["unequal"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, obsolete, usually","register":"not-comparable, obsolete, usually","wordFamily":["balanced"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:475dce859e328e04d5","definition":"Adequate; sufficiently capable or qualified.","example":"This test is pretty tough, but I think I'm equal to it.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["coordinate","equal","even","identical","level","on a par"],"antonyms":["unequal"],"collocations":[],"usage":"comparable, not-comparable, usually","register":"comparable, not-comparable, usually","w